Chapter: ProbeClosureArity2Solo

 Control for the two arity-2 probes, which produced byte-identical faults
 and so may both be failing for a reason that has nothing to do with what
 they meant to vary. Here `make2` stands alone: nothing names it.

 `solo2 53` means make2 is sound by itself and the two arity-2 probes
 really were discriminating. A fault means make2 is broken with nothing
 naming it at all, both arity-2 probes are void, and the saturation
 question is still open.

Section: Shapes

  add4 : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add4 (w) (x) (y) (z) = w + x + y + z

  make2 : Integer, Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make2 (a) (b) = (add4 a) b

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("solo2 53 expected: " & show ((((make2 5) 6) 20) 22))
  end
